       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses at that level raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and, in overdose, prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWas this a typo? Here are some options:\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the usual maximum.\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the standard starting dose, to titrate up from.\n- **Another regimen.** If you want more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, I can enter a second agent from a different class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. Tell me which drug and dose.\n\nIf you do want 30 mg daily, tell me and include the clinical rationale for the order note. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it too. Otherwise, tell me which dose to enter and I'll do it right away."
      }
